## 3. Notes on Baseline (`B0 + B1 + B2`) Verification

- **Why `[PROFILE]` shows 22 dispatches (vs 21 prior to `d6f70fb`)**:
  - Commit `d6f70fb` lowered `D3dDevice::fill`'s upload-ring `staged()` threshold to `<= 256` bytes so the per-frame 50 KB `flow_` clear (`Engine::record_net`) executes via GPU `clear_range.spv` (`~1.5 us`) instead of a PCIe DMA copy. `[PROFILE]` reports both `sum` (all 22 dispatches) and `net21_sum` (the 21 network/post dispatches excluding `clear_range.spv`).
- **B0 & K2 Deterministic SPIR-V Hash Gate**:
  - `test_asi_units.exe` computes the FNV-1a 64-bit hash of the 5 shipped Top-5 SPIR-V binaries in `build/asi/stage/openrr-amd/shaders/` and asserts `h_ship == h_nopad && h_ship != h_pad16k` (`spv_hash_nopad=EXACT`), deterministically catching any accidental re-enablement of `LDS_OCC_PAD`.
- **B1 Isolated Lossless Fast-Mode Pooling in `t0` (`attr_` Tail)**:
  - Because `enc2 .. dec2_1` execute concurrently without barriers in flow mode, `enc_l_[1].pooled` and `enc_l_[1].dfn_pool` at the start of `f0` remain live during the flow chain. Placing `dec1_l_[2..4].tensor` and `dec1_l_[1..4].dfn` in the unused tail of `t0` (`px0 * 42.4 .. px0 * 46.6 < px0 * 48`, after all `enc_l_[1..5]` sub-buffers and `dec1_l_[1].tensor`, and above `dec_head_32_64`'s `px0 * 40` `headScratch`) avoids any address overlap with live flow inputs.
  - Verified in isolation (same binary, `set_pool_dec1_tail(false)` vs `set_pool_dec1_tail(true)` across 20 frames x 2 runs): `diff_vs_unpooled=0 (max_ulp_diff=0), repeat_diff=0`, saving `1.44 MB` at 1080p (`252 -> 251 MB`), `2.5 MB` at 1440p (`438 -> 435 MB`), and `5.62 MB` at 4K (`966 -> 960 MB` feature, `-6.7 MB` `proc_delta`).
- **B2 Lossy Fast-Mode Approximations & Per-Macro A/B**:
  - Per-macro A/B in `test_asi_units.exe` confirms:
    - `post_f_lt`: `+LT_POST_EXP=1 +LT_POST_NOCORNER=1 +LT_POST_NETH=1` improves 1080p by `-12.3%` (`354.4 -> 310.9 us`) and 4K by `-2.8%` (`1436.4 -> 1396.3 us`), whereas adding `LT_POST_LOG=1` slows down 1080p by `+5.6%` (`328.4 us`) and 4K by `+6.7%` (`1489.8 us`).
    - `enc0_attr_f_lt`: `+LT_ATTR_RCP=1 +LT_ATTR_DEPTH=1` improves 1080p by `-6.7%` (`193.1 -> 180.1 us`) and 4K by `-0.5%` (`831.0 -> 826.5 us`), whereas adding `LT_ATTR_SAME=1 +LT_ATTR_CL=1` slows down 1080p by `+36.3%` (`245.4 us`) and 4K by `+19.8%` (`990.0 us`, `+163.5 us`).
    - `C=64` (`enc_stage_64_64_96` + `dec_up_64_64_96` + `dec_dfn_64_64`): `+LT_FAR=3` slows down 1080p by `+2.5%` (`708.4 -> 726.1 us`) and 4K by `+1.6%` (`2660.0 -> 2703.2 us`).
  - Note: B2 changes Fast-mode (`_lt`) numerical output relative to `d6f70fb` (`PSNR_01 = 55.53-60.40 dB`, `PSNR_tonemap = 59.93-65.17 dB`, `p99_abs_err = 0.0032-0.0054`, `non_finite = 0`), while Legacy mode (`--fast-mode 0`) remains 100% bit-exact (`max_ulp_diff = 0`).

